WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Contingency planning assumes weather, battery, communication, navigation,

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.000
or recovery conditions may change.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Identify safe landing zones, route decision points, minimum reserves, crew calls,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.000
and responsibilities before takeoff.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Loss of signal requires a site-specific response.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.325
Review configured behavior, home point, return route, altitude assumptions, terrain, wind,

00:00:19.325 --> 00:00:22.000
obstacles, and recovery-area status.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Return-to-home is a limited automation, not a guarantee.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.883
Rapid weather change may require an immediate return or landing.

00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:31.650
A strong headwind and low battery can make the planned home point less safe than a nearby

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.000
approved emergency area.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Preserve options through early thresholds and simple routes.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.415
Manual intervention may be required when automation makes an unsafe assumption or

00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:40.995
navigation becomes unreliable.

00:00:40.995 --> 00:00:45.000
Operators should act within training and procedure, communicate clearly,

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.995
and prioritize people and property over the aircraft or data.

00:00:47.995 --> 00:00:51.690
After an abnormal event, secure the area, account for people and equipment,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:54.995
preserve logs and media, inspect the aircraft, and make required notifications.

00:00:54.995 --> 00:00:59.000
Do not relaunch until weather, equipment, authorization, and cause have been reviewed.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.875
Document what happened, what cues appeared, what decisions were made,

00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:03.000
and what should change.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.350
Lessons should update thresholds, route design, training, maintenance,

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.990
and briefings without encouraging future crews to accept more risk.
